<body>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Nine Decades of Oscar-Winning Scores: A Historical Trend Analysis (1934–2026)</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A data-forward review of all 93 Best Original Score winners, with emphasis on composer concentration, decade dynamics, and era-level shifts in the Academy’s scoring canon.</p>

    <section class="panel">
      <h2>Executive KPI Snapshot</h2>
      <div class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi">
          <div class="label">Total Unique Composers</div>
          <div class="value" id="kpiUniqueComposers"></div>
          <div class="sub">Across 93 ceremonies</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi">
          <div class="label">Maximum Wins by One Composer</div>
          <div class="value" id="kpiMaxWins"></div>
          <div class="sub" id="kpiMaxWinners"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi">
          <div class="label">Repeat Winner Rate</div>
          <div class="value" id="kpiRepeatRate"></div>
          <div class="sub" id="kpiRepeatCount"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi">
          <div class="label">Decade with Most Unique Winners</div>
          <div class="value" id="kpiTopDecade"></div>
          <div class="sub" id="kpiTopDecadeCount"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Dataset Overview & Historical Context</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <p><span class="pill">Scope</span><span class="pill">1934–2026</span><span class="pill">93 ceremonies</span></p>
        <p>The dataset contains one winning film-composer record per ceremony year, yielding a continuous historical series from 1934 to 2026. It includes <strong id="uniqueFilms"></strong> unique winning film titles and <strong id="uniqueComposers"></strong> distinct credited composer entries.</p>
        <p class="note">Method note: analyses reflect the exact `Composer` strings in the source CSV, including co-credit entries represented as a single combined string.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Most Awarded Composers</h2>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="topComposersChart"></canvas></div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>Interpretation</h3>
          <p>The leaderboard shows a narrow top tier. Three composers are tied at the historical ceiling, indicating that “all-time dominance” is shared rather than monopolized.</p>
          <p>Below the top tier, win counts drop quickly to three and then two, suggesting a long-tail structure where many composers win once while a small core repeats.</p>
          <table id="topComposerTable"></table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Temporal Patterns & Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</h2>
      <div class="grid-2-eq">
        <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="decadeUniqueChart"></canvas></div>
        <div class="chart-wrap small"><canvas id="decadeConcentrationChart"></canvas></div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Decade Dynamics</h3>
        <ul id="decadeNarrative"></ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Era-Based Analysis of Winning Scores</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <p>To preserve analytical consistency with the brief, eras are approximated from ceremony years:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Golden Age (1934–1959):</strong> studio-system orchestral tradition, recurrent late-romantic symphonic writing.</li>
          <li><strong>Silver Age (1960–1979):</strong> broader stylistic range, including jazz/pop influences and franchise leitmotif emergence.</li>
          <li><strong>Modern (1980–1999):</strong> increased blend of orchestral and hybrid textures, plus animated-musical resurgence.</li>
          <li><strong>Contemporary (2000–2026):</strong> hybrid production aesthetics, stronger global stylistic spread, and faster repeat cycles for select composers.</li>
        </ul>
        <table id="eraTable"></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Notable Milestones & Records</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <ul id="milestones"></ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Key Takeaways & Forward-Looking Observations</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <ul class="takeaways" id="takeaways"></ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="footer">Source: `/app/benchmark/data.csv` (93 records). Report generated as a self-contained HTML artifact.</p>
  </div>

  <script>
    const data = [
      {"Year":1934,"Film":"One Night of Love","Composer":"Louis Silvers"},{"Year":1935,"Film":"The Informer","Composer":"Max Steiner"},{"Year":1936,"Film":"Anthony Adverse","Composer":"Leo F. Forbstein"},{"Year":1937,"Film":"One Hundred Men and a Girl","Composer":"Charles Previn"},{"Year":1938,"Film":"The Adventures of Robin Hood","Composer":"Erich Wolfgang Korngold"},{"Year":1939,"Film":"Stagecoach","Composer":"Richard Hageman, W. Franke Harling, John Leipold, Leo Shuken"},{"Year":1940,"Film":"The Wizard of Oz","Composer":"Herbert Stothart"},{"Year":1941,"Film":"Pinocchio","Composer":"Leigh Harline, Paul J. Smith, Ned Washington"},{"Year":1942,"Film":"Dumbo","Composer":"Frank Churchill, Oliver Wallace"},{"Year":1943,"Film":"Now, Voyager","Composer":"Max Steiner"},{"Year":1944,"Film":"The Song of Bernadette","Composer":"Alfred Newman"},{"Year":1945,"Film":"Since You Went Away","Composer":"Max Steiner"},{"Year":1946,"Film":"Spellbound","Composer":"Miklos Rozsa"},{"Year":1947,"Film":"The Best Years of Our Lives","Composer":"Hugo Friedhofer"},{"Year":1948,"Film":"The Red Shoes","Composer":"Brian Easdale"},{"Year":1949,"Film":"The Heiress","Composer":"Aaron Copland"},{"Year":1950,"Film":"Sunset Boulevard","Composer":"Franz Waxman"},{"Year":1951,"Film":"A Place in the Sun","Composer":"Franz Waxman"},{"Year":1952,"Film":"High Noon","Composer":"Dimitri Tiomkin"},{"Year":1953,"Film":"Lili","Composer":"Bronislau Kaper"},{"Year":1954,"Film":"The High and the Mighty","Composer":"Dimitri Tiomkin"},{"Year":1955,"Film":"Love Is a Many-Splendored Thing","Composer":"Alfred Newman"},{"Year":1956,"Film":"Around the World in 80 Days","Composer":"Victor Young"},{"Year":1957,"Film":"The Bridge on the River Kwai","Composer":"Malcolm Arnold"},{"Year":1958,"Film":"The Old Man and the Sea","Composer":"Dimitri Tiomkin"},{"Year":1959,"Film":"Ben-Hur","Composer":"Miklos Rozsa"},{"Year":1960,"Film":"Exodus","Composer":"Ernest Gold"},{"Year":1961,"Film":"Breakfast at Tiffany's","Composer":"Henry Mancini"},{"Year":1962,"Film":"Lawrence of Arabia","Composer":"Maurice Jarre"},{"Year":1963,"Film":"Tom Jones","Composer":"John Addison"},{"Year":1964,"Film":"Mary Poppins","Composer":"Richard M. Sherman, Robert B. Sherman"},{"Year":1965,"Film":"Doctor Zhivago","Composer":"Maurice Jarre"},{"Year":1966,"Film":"Born Free","Composer":"John Barry"},{"Year":1967,"Film":"Thoroughly Modern Millie","Composer":"Elmer Bernstein"},{"Year":1968,"Film":"The Lion in Winter","Composer":"John Barry"},{"Year":1969,"Film":"Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid","Composer":"Burt Bacharach"},{"Year":1970,"Film":"Love Story","Composer":"Francis Lai"},{"Year":1971,"Film":"Summer of '42","Composer":"Michel Legrand"},{"Year":1972,"Film":"The Godfather","Composer":"Nino Rota"},{"Year":1973,"Film":"The Way We Were","Composer":"Marvin Hamlisch"},{"Year":1974,"Film":"The Godfather Part II","Composer":"Nino Rota, Carmine Coppola"},{"Year":1975,"Film":"Jaws","Composer":"John Williams"},{"Year":1976,"Film":"The Omen","Composer":"Jerry Goldsmith"},{"Year":1977,"Film":"Star Wars","Composer":"John Williams"},{"Year":1978,"Film":"Midnight Express","Composer":"Giorgio Moroder"},{"Year":1979,"Film":"A Little Romance","Composer":"Georges Delerue"},{"Year":1980,"Film":"Fame","Composer":"Michael Gore"},{"Year":1981,"Film":"Chariots of Fire","Composer":"Vangelis"},{"Year":1982,"Film":"E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial","Composer":"John Williams"},{"Year":1983,"Film":"The Right Stuff","Composer":"Bill Conti"},{"Year":1984,"Film":"A Passage to India","Composer":"Maurice Jarre"},{"Year":1985,"Film":"Out of Africa","Composer":"John Barry"},{"Year":1986,"Film":"Round Midnight","Composer":"Herbie Hancock"},{"Year":1987,"Film":"The Last Emperor","Composer":"Ryuichi Sakamoto, David Byrne, Cong Su"},{"Year":1988,"Film":"The Milagro Beanfield War","Composer":"Dave Grusin"},{"Year":1989,"Film":"The Little Mermaid","Composer":"Alan Menken"},{"Year":1990,"Film":"Dances with Wolves","Composer":"John Barry"},{"Year":1991,"Film":"Beauty and the Beast","Composer":"Alan Menken"},{"Year":1992,"Film":"Aladdin","Composer":"Alan Menken"},{"Year":1993,"Film":"Schindler's List","Composer":"John Williams"},{"Year":1994,"Film":"The Lion King","Composer":"Hans Zimmer"},{"Year":1995,"Film":"The Postman","Composer":"Luis Bacalov"},{"Year":1996,"Film":"The English Patient","Composer":"Gabriel Yared"},{"Year":1997,"Film":"Titanic","Composer":"James Horner"},{"Year":1998,"Film":"Life Is Beautiful","Composer":"Nicola Piovani"},{"Year":1999,"Film":"The Red Violin","Composer":"John Corigliano"},{"Year":2000,"Film":"Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon","Composer":"Tan Dun"},{"Year":2001,"Film":"The Lord of the Rings: The Fellowship of the Ring","Composer":"Howard Shore"},{"Year":2002,"Film":"Frida","Composer":"Elliot Goldenthal"},{"Year":2003,"Film":"The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King","Composer":"Howard Shore"},{"Year":2004,"Film":"Finding Neverland","Composer":"Jan A.P. Kaczmarek"},{"Year":2005,"Film":"Brokeback Mountain","Composer":"Gustavo Santaolalla"},{"Year":2006,"Film":"Babel","Composer":"Gustavo Santaolalla"},{"Year":2007,"Film":"Atonement","Composer":"Dario Marianelli"},{"Year":2008,"Film":"Slumdog Millionaire","Composer":"A.R. Rahman"},{"Year":2009,"Film":"Up","Composer":"Michael Giacchino"},{"Year":2010,"Film":"The Social Network","Composer":"Trent Reznor, Atticus Ross"},{"Year":2011,"Film":"The Artist","Composer":"Ludovic Bource"},{"Year":2012,"Film":"Life of Pi","Composer":"Mychael Danna"},{"Year":2013,"Film":"Gravity","Composer":"Steven Price"},{"Year":2014,"Film":"The Grand Budapest Hotel","Composer":"Alexandre Desplat"},{"Year":2015,"Film":"The Hateful Eight","Composer":"Ennio Morricone"},{"Year":2016,"Film":"La La Land","Composer":"Justin Hurwitz"},{"Year":2017,"Film":"The Shape of Water","Composer":"Alexandre Desplat"},{"Year":2018,"Film":"Black Panther","Composer":"Ludwig Göransson"},{"Year":2019,"Film":"Joker","Composer":"Hildur Guðnadóttir"},{"Year":2020,"Film":"Soul","Composer":"Trent Reznor, Atticus Ross, Jon Batiste"},{"Year":2021,"Film":"Dune","Composer":"Hans Zimmer"},{"Year":2022,"Film":"All Quiet on the Western Front","Composer":"Volker Bertelmann"},{"Year":2023,"Film":"Oppenheimer","Composer":"Ludwig Göransson"},{"Year":2024,"Film":"Oppenheimer","Composer":"Ludwig Göransson"},{"Year":2025,"Film":"The Brutalist","Composer":"Daniel Blumberg"},{"Year":2026,"Film":"Sinners","Composer":"Ludwig Göransson"}
    ];

    const byComposer = data.reduce((m, d) => (m[d.Composer] = (m[d.Composer] || 0) + 1, m), {});
    const composerEntries = Object.entries(byComposer).sort((a,b)=>b[1]-a[1] || a[0].localeCompare(b[0]));

    const total = data.length;
    const uniqueComposers = Object.keys(byComposer).length;
    const uniqueFilms = new Set(data.map(d=>d.Film)).size;
    const maxWins = composerEntries[0][1];
    const maxWinners = composerEntries.filter(([_,w]) => w===maxWins).map(([c])=>c);

    const sorted = [...data].sort((a,b)=>a.Year-b.Year);
    let seen = new Set();
    let repeatCount = 0;
    sorted.forEach(r => { if (seen.has(r.Composer)) repeatCount++; seen.add(r.Composer); });
    const repeatRate = repeatCount / total;

    const decade = y => Math.floor(y/10)*10;
    const decadeMap = {};
    sorted.forEach(r => {
      const d = decade(r.Year);
      if (!decadeMap[d]) decadeMap[d] = {rows:[], composers:new Set()};
      decadeMap[d].rows.push(r);
      decadeMap[d].composers.add(r.Composer);
    });

    const decades = Object.keys(decadeMap).map(Number).sort((a,b)=>a-b);
    const decadeUniqueCounts = decades.map(d => decadeMap[d].composers.size);
    const topDecadeCount = Math.max(...decadeUniqueCounts);
    const topDecade = decades[decadeUniqueCounts.indexOf(topDecadeCount)];

    const decadeRepeatShare = decades.map(d => {
      const counts = {};
      decadeMap[d].rows.forEach(r => counts[r.Composer] = (counts[r.Composer]||0)+1);
      const repeatedWins = Object.values(counts).filter(v=>v>1).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
      return +(repeatedWins / decadeMap[d].rows.length * 100).toFixed(1);
    });

    document.getElementById('kpiUniqueComposers').textContent = uniqueComposers;
    document.getElementById('kpiMaxWins').textContent = maxWins;
    document.getElementById('kpiMaxWinners').textContent = maxWinners.join(' • ');
    document.getElementById('kpiRepeatRate').textContent = (repeatRate*100).toFixed(1) + '%';
    document.getElementById('kpiRepeatCount').textContent = `${repeatCount} of ${total} ceremonies`;
    document.getElementById('kpiTopDecade').textContent = `${topDecade}s`;
    document.getElementById('kpiTopDecadeCount').textContent = `${topDecadeCount} unique winners`;
    document.getElementById('uniqueFilms').textContent = uniqueFilms;
    document.getElementById('uniqueComposers').textContent = uniqueComposers;

    const top10 = composerEntries.slice(0,10);
    new Chart(document.getElementById('topComposersChart'), {
      type: 'bar',
      data: {
        labels: top10.map(([c])=>c),
        datasets: [{
          label: 'Wins',
          data: top10.map(([_,w])=>w),
          backgroundColor: '#ffd166',
          borderColor: '#ffbf3f',
          borderWidth: 1
        }]
      },
      options: {
        responsive: true,
        plugins: { legend: { display: false }, title: { display: true, text: 'Top 10 Most Awarded Composer Credits' } },
        scales: {
          x: { ticks: { color: '#dce4ff', maxRotation: 55, minRotation: 30 }, grid: { color: '#26345e' } },
          y: { ticks: { color: '#dce4ff', precision: 0 }, grid: { color: '#26345e' }, beginAtZero: true }
        }
      }
    });

    new Chart(document.getElementById('decadeUniqueChart'), {
      type: 'line',
      data: {
        labels: decades.map(d=>`${d}s`),
        datasets: [{
          label: 'Unique winning composer entries',
          data: decadeUniqueCounts,
          borderColor: '#7bdff2',
          pointBackgroundColor: '#7bdff2',
          tension: 0.25,
          fill: false
        }]
      },
      options: {
        plugins: { title: { display: true, text: 'Diversity of Winners by Decade' }, legend: { labels: { color: '#dce4ff' } } },
        scales: {
          x: { ticks: { color: '#dce4ff' }, grid: { color: '#26345e' } },
          y: { ticks: { color: '#dce4ff', precision: 0 }, grid: { color: '#26345e' }, beginAtZero: true }
        }
      }
    });

    new Chart(document.getElementById('decadeConcentrationChart'), {
      type: 'bar',
      data: {
        labels: decades.map(d=>`${d}s`),
        datasets: [{
          label: '% of decade wins by repeat winners within decade',
          data: decadeRepeatShare,
          backgroundColor: '#b2f7ef'
        }]
      },
      options: {
        plugins: { title: { display: true, text: 'Within-Decade Concentration (Repeat Share)' }, legend: { labels: { color: '#dce4ff' } } },
        scales: {
          x: { ticks: { color: '#dce4ff' }, grid: { color: '#26345e' } },
          y: { ticks: { color: '#dce4ff' }, grid: { color: '#26345e' }, beginAtZero: true, max: 100 }
        }
      }
    });

    const topTable = document.getElementById('topComposerTable');
    const rows = composerEntries.slice(0,12).map(([c,w],i)=>`<tr><td>${i+1}</td><td>${c}</td><td>${w}</td></tr>`).join('');
    topTable.innerHTML = `<thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Composer</th><th>Wins</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows}</tbody>`;

    const dn = document.getElementById('decadeNarrative');
    const highestRepeatDecadeIdx = decadeRepeatShare.indexOf(Math.max(...decadeRepeatShare));
    const lowestRepeatDecadeIdx = decadeRepeatShare.indexOf(Math.min(...decadeRepeatShare));
    dn.innerHTML = [
      `<li><strong>Peak diversity:</strong> the ${topDecade}s produced ${topDecadeCount} unique winners, the broadest composer turnover in the full series.</li>`,
      `<li><strong>Most concentrated decade:</strong> the ${decades[highestRepeatDecadeIdx]}s show the highest within-decade repeat share at ${decadeRepeatShare[highestRepeatDecadeIdx]}%, indicating stronger winner recurrence.</li>`,
      `<li><strong>Most open decade:</strong> the ${decades[lowestRepeatDecadeIdx]}s record the lowest repeat share at ${decadeRepeatShare[lowestRepeatDecadeIdx]}%, reflecting the weakest short-window concentration.</li>`,
      `<li><strong>Long-run balance:</strong> despite headline repeat winners, ${uniqueComposers} unique composer entries across ${total} years indicate that one-off wins remain the modal outcome.</li>`
    ].join('');

    const eras = [
      {name:'Golden Age', from:1934, to:1959},
      {name:'Silver Age', from:1960, to:1979},
      {name:'Modern', from:1980, to:1999},
      {name:'Contemporary', from:2000, to:2026},
    ];
    const eraRows = eras.map(e => {
      const rows = sorted.filter(r=>r.Year>=e.from && r.Year<=e.to);
      const counts = {};
      rows.forEach(r=>counts[r.Composer]=(counts[r.Composer]||0)+1);
      const max = Math.max(...Object.values(counts));
      const leaders = Object.entries(counts).filter(([_,w])=>w===max).map(([c])=>c).join('; ');
      return `<tr><td>${e.name} (${e.from}–${e.to})</td><td>${rows.length}</td><td>${new Set(rows.map(r=>r.Composer)).size}</td><td>${leaders} (${max})</td></tr>`;
    }).join('');
    document.getElementById('eraTable').innerHTML = `<thead><tr><th>Era</th><th>Ceremonies</th><th>Unique Winners</th><th>Most Frequent Winner(s)</th></tr></thead><tbody>${eraRows}</tbody>`;

    const longestGaps = [];
    Object.keys(byComposer).forEach(c => {
      const ys = sorted.filter(r=>r.Composer===c).map(r=>r.Year);
      for (let i=1;i<ys.length;i++) longestGaps.push({composer:c,from:ys[i-1],to:ys[i],gap:ys[i]-ys[i-1]});
    });
    longestGaps.sort((a,b)=>b.gap-a.gap);

    const firstWinner = sorted[0];
    const latestWinner = sorted[sorted.length-1];
    document.getElementById('milestones').innerHTML = [
      `<li><strong>First recorded winner in this dataset:</strong> ${firstWinner.Composer} for <em>${firstWinner.Film}</em> (${firstWinner.Year}).</li>`,
      `<li><strong>Most recent winner:</strong> ${latestWinner.Composer} for <em>${latestWinner.Film}</em> (${latestWinner.Year}).</li>`,
      `<li><strong>All-time maximum wins:</strong> ${maxWins}, shared by ${maxWinners.join(', ')}.</li>`,
      `<li><strong>Longest gap between wins (same composer credit):</strong> ${longestGaps[0].gap} years (${longestGaps[0].composer}, ${longestGaps[0].from} to ${longestGaps[0].to}).</li>`,
      `<li><strong>Early-career turnover signal:</strong> ${total - repeatCount} ceremonies (${((1-repeatRate)*100).toFixed(1)}%) were won by composers at their first win point in the timeline.</li>`
    ].join('');

    document.getElementById('takeaways').innerHTML = [
      `<li>The Oscar score canon combines <strong>elite recurrence</strong> (a small top tier with 4 wins) and <strong>broad participation</strong> (${uniqueComposers} unique winners over ${total} years).</li>`,
      `<li>Decade-level diversity peaks in the <strong>${topDecade}s</strong>, indicating periodic resets where new names break through despite historical incumbents.</li>`,
      `<li>Repeat-winner dynamics are cyclical rather than linear: concentration rises in some decades but recedes in others, showing that Academy preferences are not locked to a single composer cohort.</li>`,
      `<li>The Contemporary era (2000–2026) shows rapid cycles of recognition, including recent multi-win acceleration by Ludwig Göransson through 2026.</li>`,
      `<li>Looking toward the late 2020s, the baseline pattern suggests continued tension between franchise-era repeat visibility and ongoing first-time winner entry.</li>`
    ].join('');
  </script>
</body>
</html>
